# Allowlist, not a denylist. The previous denylist let 216MB of vendored ENHSP
# source (with its own .git), editor backups of deleted files, local pipeline
# logs carrying absolute home paths, and a stale uv.lock into a published public
# image — because `docker build` copies the working tree, not the commit, so
# anything lying around untracked ships. Listing what the image needs fails
# closed instead: new junk is excluded by default.
*

# Container entrypoint and the three pipeline stages it chains.
!main.py
!docker-entrypoint.sh
!convert_to_pddl/
!convert_plan_to_tors/
!plan/

# The visualizer mode of the entrypoint.
!plan_visualizer/

# Deliberately kept: lets the suite run inside the image, which is the only
# place the Julia backend is instantiated. ~52K.
!tests/
!pytest.ini

!requirements.txt
!requirements-test.txt

# Re-exclude things the recursive includes above would drag back in.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/*~
**/.pytest_cache/
tools/planners/enhsp/.git/
